WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:03.250
Ready for a serious case of the heebie-jeebies?

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:08.519
Sony Pictures has released the first official
poster for its upcoming remake/reboot/sequel

00:00:08.519 --> 00:00:12.330
The Grudge, and we sincerely hope that you're
not about to jump in the shower.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:17.690
The one-sheet references an iconic scene from
the 2004 film that has literally never stopped

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:18.830
giving us the creeps.

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:24.160
In case you're not familiar, that flick itself
a remake of the 2002 Japanese film Ju-On:

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:29.510
The Grudge starred Sarah Michelle Gellar as
Karen Davis, an American exchange student

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:33.640
in Japan who moves into a house populated
by malevolent spirits.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:38.370
These are no run-of-the-mill spooks, however;
they're an extra-virulent variety created

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:43.929
when one dies under extraordinarily emotional
circumstances, and as the flick's title implies,

00:00:43.929 --> 00:00:46.040
they don't go away... ever.

00:00:52.409 --> 00:00:56.840
In the scene in question, Karen is enjoying
a nice, hot shower, and is in the middle of

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:01.979
washing her hair when she suddenly appears
to grow an extra hand... from the back of

00:01:01.979 --> 00:01:02.979
her head.

00:01:02.979 --> 00:01:07.610
It's an incredibly unnerving jump scare, and
the fact that the new flick's producers chose

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:11.670
to invoke it for their movie's first poster
tells us something about the specific vein

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.450
of terror they're hoping to mine.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:18.740
As the poster notes, Sam Raimi, who served
as a producer on the 2004 film and the first

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:22.170
of its two sequels, is back in that role for
this go-round.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:27.189
He's got an interesting talent in the director's
chair: Nicolas Pesce who turned in low-key,

00:01:27.189 --> 00:01:32.909
slow-burn, minor masterpieces with 2016's
Eyes of My Mother and 2018's Piercing.

00:01:32.909 --> 00:01:36.920
According to Pesce, his film will more than
make good on this poster's promise to scare

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:38.549
the absolute hell out of you.

00:01:38.549 --> 00:01:42.700
The director has explained that he views The
Grudge as, quote, "an anthology series...

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:47.729
[featuring] different characters, different
stories, different locations, different ghosts,"

00:01:47.729 --> 00:01:51.900
and while he is taking care to stay true to
what came before, he promises that when it

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:56.609
comes to the level of pure terror he's going
for, audiences simply aren't ready.

00:01:56.609 --> 00:01:58.860
Pesce told a crowd at New York Comic-Con:

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:03.409
"The movie's way more f----d up [than the
other films in the series].

00:02:03.409 --> 00:02:08.369
Not that the wave of J-Horror in the early
2000s wasn't f----d up — but this is really

00:02:08.369 --> 00:02:09.369
f----d up."

00:02:09.369 --> 00:02:13.850
Pesce went on to explain that he rejects the
"reboot" label, as his Grudge takes place

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:18.730
in the same timeline as the 2004 movie, and
that he is in no way simply telling a different

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:20.260
version of the same story.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:21.260
He explained:

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:23.650
"We're not rehashing [the first film].

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:27.970
We're finding the key elements that are just
how the grudge expresses itself.

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:32.760
So much of this movie is about the fact that
this can happen anywhere and that it happens

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:33.760
everywhere.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:35.549
It can spread like wildfire.

00:02:35.549 --> 00:02:37.709
Having certain touchstones was important.

00:02:37.709 --> 00:02:40.909
Obviously with a franchise we don't want to
throw everything out.

00:02:40.909 --> 00:02:45.330
There is certain stuff that is fun for the
fans to see again in a new context with a

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:46.330
new spin."

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:51.489
The director also let slip a few details about
the flick's plot in a conversation with Entertainment

00:02:51.489 --> 00:02:52.489
Weekly.

00:02:52.489 --> 00:02:56.760
It will focus on a police officer played by
Mandy's Andrea Riseborough who arrives in

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:02.439
a new town only to be handed a bizarre and
inexplicable case one which leads her to investigate

00:03:02.439 --> 00:03:07.170
a mysterious house that, as Pesce describes
it, quote, "has been grudged."

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:08.849
The director explained:

00:03:08.849 --> 00:03:14.180
"We follow her, as well as two other storylines,
that are all interacting with this 'grudged'

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:16.019
house in small town America.

00:03:16.019 --> 00:03:20.101
Like the old films, it's a tapestry of three
different stories that interweave and all

00:03:20.101 --> 00:03:24.860
take place at slightly different times, centered
around this one house that's at the center

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:27.530
of this case that this cop is working on."

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:31.430
That sounds really cool, but we're going to
need a bit more confirmation on the movie's

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:32.430
fright factor.

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:36.310
Let's check in with horror legend Lin Shaye,
who is also appearing in the film, and who

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:40.379
had a few choice words when asked about the
project in an interview with ComicBook.

00:03:40.379 --> 00:03:41.379
Shaye dished:

00:03:41.379 --> 00:03:43.329
"Wait until you see this.

00:03:43.329 --> 00:03:47.590
It's the scariest movie I've ever been a part
of, not even maybe.

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:48.890
Not even maybe.

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:52.210
It's the scariest part I've ever had, bar
none...

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:53.930
I'm very excited about it.

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:57.840
The horror fans are going to go insane, that
I can promise."

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:01.069
Okay, that's all we needed, we're officially
on board.

00:04:01.069 --> 00:04:06.719
In addition to Riseborough and Shaye, The
Grudge stars Betty Gilpin, John Cho, William

00:04:06.719 --> 00:04:08.780
Sadler, and Demian Bichir.

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:12.840
The haunting flick will hit screens on January
3, 2020.

